  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Why these conversions are exact</h2>
    <p>U.S. customary units are defined in terms of metric ones. Since an international agreement in 1959, the inch has been exactly 2.54 centimeters and the pound exactly 0.45359237 kilograms. Every other U.S. length, area, volume, and weight unit follows from those definitions, so conversions like 1 mile = 1,609.344 meters or 1 U.S. gallon = 3.785411784 liters are exact, not measured approximations. The converters here use these defined factors and round only the displayed result.</p>

    <h2>The conversions people get wrong most</h2>
  </div>
